## What Changed

### Audio Quality Fix: Click-Free Stop Commands

Fixed audio popping/clicking issue when stopping samples via StopAll and VoiceStop
commands. These commands now apply a brief 10ms fade-out before removing samples,
preventing waveform discontinuities that cause audible clicks.

**Root Cause:** Immediate sample removal would cut audio mid-waveform, creating
sharp discontinuities (e.g., jumping from +0.3 amplitude to 0.0) which manifest
as clicks/pops.

**Fix:** All stop commands (StopAll, VoiceStop) now apply a 10ms automatic fade-out
before removal. This is imperceptible to users but ensures smooth ramp to zero,
eliminating clicks entirely.

**Changed files:**
- src/main.rs: Updated StopAll and VoiceStop handlers to apply fade-out
  instead of immediate removal

